  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "LuciferCore High-Performance HTTP Refactoring\n\n      - This release introduces strict case-sensitive HTTP parsing per RFC standards. Methods and routing now require standard uppercase tokens (e.g., GET, PUT), eliminating runtime normalization overhead and dropping lookup complexity from O(k) to deterministic O(1).\n      - The static routing pipeline has been stripped of legacy fallback heuristics like auto-appending .html extensions. It now exclusively serves exact dictionary matches via Mapping or direct paths extracted before the query separator, offloading all magic routing to the API layer.\n      - The socket loop introduces an adaptive dynamic request lifecycle. A single RequestModel is bound inline to the connection, using fast .Clear() resets for zero-allocation pipeline batching, and immediately disposing back to the pool when the connection is idle.",
